      {
        "@language": "fr",
        "@value": "Women-led ensemble Bel and Quinn captivate with their magnificent musical arrangements and a trilingual poetic discourse imbued with sensitivity. Their songs fuse Haitian rhythms, jazz, soul and funk in a cry fighting against the stigmatization of mental illnesses. They offer their songs to their audiences as an act of healing, love and self-acceptance. Committed to promoting female artists, the duo is accompanied on stage by talented musicians. The duo's shows are a celebration where the two sisters of Haitian origin establish themselves as women, black, and musicians."
      }
    ],
